      "content": "4. Major Canals & Irrigation Projects"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Karoh Peak (1,499 metres) in the Morni Hills of Panchkula district is the highest point in Haryana.",
        "Dhosi Hill (652 metres) in Mahendragarh district represents an extinct volcano and the highest elevation of the Aravalli range within Haryana.",
        "The Saraswati, Ghaggar, Markanda, and Tangri rivers belong to the northern seasonal drainage system originating in the Shivalik ranges.",
        "Western Yamuna Canal is the oldest canal system in the state, originally dug during the reign of Sultan Firoz Shah Tughlaq in the 14th century."
      ],
      "id": "0h84dy9"
